1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,680
I was eight. Grandma had bought my aunt a long wall sweeper.

2
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:11,780
I could not take my eyes off it. "Whose will it be?" I kept wondering.

3
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:15,740
The next morning, my eyes still never left the sweeper.

4
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:26,180
At ten, dressed in black for mourning, Grandma set off to comfort grieving neighbours. "I'll be right back, my child," she said.

5
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:31,860
But I thought she said, "Bring the sweeper and follow me."

6
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:39,320
So I put the sweeper on my shoulder and followed her. I was behind, so she never saw me.

7
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:44,940
I even crossed the asphalt road, the sweeper still on my shoulder.

8
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:49,860
Grandma had only just sat down in the house of mourning…

9
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,200
…when I appeared at the door.

10
00:00:56,300 --> 00:01:02,000
Startled, Grandma hurried to me, wondering how I had ever crossed that road.

11
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:08,360
Then she laughed, and called my aunt to take me, and her sweeper, back home.

12
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:18,660
My dear grandmother is no longer with us. But this story makes our family and our neighbours laugh. It still does.
